<article class="env-lemma" id="0BCM">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BCM">Lemma <span data-tag="0BCM">31.11.7</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a flat morphism of schemes. If $Y$ is integral and the generic fibre of $f$ is integral, then $X$ is integral. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The algebraic analogue is this: let $A$ be a domain with fraction field $K$ and let $B$ be a flat $A$-algebra such that $B \otimes _ A K$ is a domain. Then $B$ is a domain. This is true because $B$ is torsion free by More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0538" data-tag="0538">15.22.9</a> and hence $B \subset B \otimes _ A K$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>